    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d77">

                <pb facs="0187" n="81" sameAs="frus:frus1891/pg81"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Pacheco to Mr. Blaine</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States in Guatemala and
                                Honduras</hi>.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-09-17"><hi rendition="#italic">September 17,
                            1891</hi>.</date> (Received September 19.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Pacheco states that under the law of Salvador a vessel leaving port without
                    clearance papers is subject to confiscation; that the Salvadorian minister for
                    foreign affairs had been asked by telegraph how long the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >City of Panama</hi> can be detained under the contract, but no answer has
                    been received; and that this may be due to the continual interruption of the
                    wires.</p>
            </div>
